From 673fedf2bf814f8238894f1dafe9b65472c9719f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:27:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(spec_decode): guard negative copy slots, step down cap
 gently, and unlock 31/63-token copy ramp

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
1. copy_match_kernel guarded slot >= 0 before reading total_len[slot], whereas copy_alloc_kernel and copy_apply_kernel indexed total_len[slot], int_state[slot], float_state[slot], and history[slot] unconditionally even when idx_mapping contained negative padded slots.
2. When a copy proposal of length live > initial was partially accepted (initial <= accepted < live, such as 15/16 on a single edited token inside a copied block), copy_alloc_kernel reset doublings = 0 all the way back to initial (4), requiring three consecutive full-cap steps (4 -> 8 -> 16) to recover lookahead.
3. In copy_match_kernel, each candidate tile probed every ladder level 0..count-1 without checking the target level anchor token history[slot, e - levels[i]] == key[levels[i] - 1] first, walked tiles below need_len, and executed 5 * count = 25 warp shfl_xor reductions on every hit tile even when only hit[0] was needed to test tile emptiness.
4. greedy_rejection_kernel in tilelang_sampling.py restricted width <= 32 (max_drafts <= 31), preventing greedy speculative verification from evaluating max_drafts = 63 (64 total rows = 1 decode_64 MMA tile and 1 DECODE_CHUNK = 64 indexer wave) even though copy_apply_kernel, assign_draft_budget_kernel, and verify_kernel already support up to 64 drafts.

Guard slot >= 0 in copy_alloc_kernel and copy_apply_kernel; step doublings down by 1 (T.max(doublings - 1, 0)) when initial <= accepted < live while resetting doublings = 0 when accepted < initial; add the level-anchor probe, need_len tile bound, and 1-variable hit[0] warp reduction in copy_match_kernel; and support multi-pass width <= 65 in greedy_rejection_kernel alongside SPARK_DS41F_COPY_MAX_DRAFTS in SpeculativeConfig and --lookahead in benchmark_copy_drafts.py.

Quality:
Bit-exact match selection and greedy rejection semantics for all valid slots; prevents out-of-bounds global memory reads/writes on negative padded slots, speeds up 16-256K suffix matching by up to 1.18x on boilerplate-heavy histories, and unlocks 31- and 63-token copy lookahead ramps (1.85x and 3.53x fewer decode steps on 2,048-token verbatim copies; 1.32x and 1.47x fewer decode steps on spliced copies).

Tests:
- pytest --noconftest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_copy_drafts.py tests/v1/core/test_copy_drafts_scheduler.py (63 passed across 2 container boots on GB10).
- python3 benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_copy_drafts.py --gate (0 slower across all 12 cells across 2 container boots on GB10).

Upstream status: local speculative decoding optimization for unified-memory GB10 nodes.
